How to run react application in Jenkins?
1. Create a jenkins file named Jenkinsfile in root directory where package.json exist.
2. Add content for the Jenkinfile
 
pipeline {
    agent any

    stages {
        stage('Checkout') {
            steps {
                git url: 'https://github.com/shreerakshabm99/frontendapp.git', branch: 'dev'
            }
        }

        stage('Install Dependencies') {
            steps {
                dir('login-app') {
                    // Install project dependencies including sonar-scanner
                    bat 'npm install'
       
                }
            }
        }

        stage('Build') {
            steps {
                dir('login-app') {
                    bat 'npm run build'
                }
            }
       }



        stage('Archive Build') {
            steps {
                dir('login-app') {
                    archiveArtifacts artifacts: 'build/**', fingerprint: true
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
3. Push the project into git 
4. Open Jenkin and create a new item, Give a name to the project and select pipeline and click OK.
5. Move to Configure and give a description.
6. In pipeline section add definition as Pipeline script from scm
7. Add the Repository Url and add the Credentials.
8. Mention the branch where the project is present in git(example: dev)
9. Provide the correct script path where Jenkinsfile is present.
10. Click on apply and save.
11. Click on BuildRun and check the console output.


----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
How to configure SonarQube in Jenkins?

1. Download community version of SonarQube and extract it in Cdrive.
2. move to C/SonarQube/bin/windowsx86-64 folder and open cmd and type StartSonar.bat (It will open SonarQube)
3. The default login and password is admin and later change the password.
4. Click on My account->security->provide name and select user token and then click on generate.
5. copy the token 
6. In Jenkins->plugins->available plugins-> search SonarQube and install all the available plugins.
7. In jenkins->settings->credentials->select global->select add credentials->select kind as secret text->paste the token in secret field-> give a name in the id field->click on create
8. in jenkins->go to system->search for SonarQube servers->give name and url and select server authentication token as the name similar to the id given in credentials.
9.save
10. In React project, create a sonar-project.properties file in the root directory where package.json exis.
11.Add the below content in this file
sonar.projectKey=react-app
sonar.projectName=React App
sonar.projectVersion=1.0
sonar.sources=src
sonar.sourceEncoding=UTF-8
sonar.exclusions=**/node_modules/**,**/build/**,**/*.test.js,**/*.spec.js
sonar.javascript.lcov.reportPaths=coverage/lcov.info
12. Add the below content in jenkinsfile
pipeline {
    agent any

    stages {
        stage('Checkout') {
            steps {
                git url: 'https://github.com/shreerakshabm99/frontendapp.git', branch: 'dev'
            }
        }

        stage('Install Dependencies') {
            steps {
                dir('login-app') {
                    // Install project dependencies including sonar-scanner
                    bat 'npm install'
                    // Also install sonar-scanner locally (if not already in package.json)
                    bat 'npm install --save-dev sonar-scanner'
                }
            }
        }

        stage('Build') {
            steps {
                dir('login-app') {
                    bat 'npm run build'
                }
            }
        }



  stage('Test') {
  steps {
    dir('login-app') {
      bat 'npm test'
    }
  }
}



        stage('SonarQube Analysis') {
            steps {
                dir('login-app') {
                    withSonarQubeEnv('SonarQube Server') {
                        // Use local sonar-scanner from node_modules
                        bat '.\\node_modules\\.bin\\sonar-scanner.cmd'
                    }
                }
            }
        }

        stage('Archive Build') {
            steps {
                dir('login-app') {
                    archiveArtifacts artifacts: 'build/**', fingerprint: true
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
13. In package.json add "sonar-scanner" under the scripts part. 
14. In Jenkins under the pipeline project, Click on Build Run and move to console output and open the link given in the console output to see the SonarQube dashboard.


